`api_endpoint` (`lib/WWW/Picnic.pm:122`) is `https://storefront-prod.<country>.picnicinternational.com/...`; there is no plain-HTTP variant. `cpanfile` lists `JSON::MaybeXS`, `HTTP::Message`, `LWP::UserAgent`, `Moo`. `LWP::Protocol::https` is a separate distribution, so a clean install answers the first call with `501 Protocol scheme 'https' is not supported`, reported as `login failed! 501 ...`. (p5-www-metaforge fixed the same in its k5.)

`URI` is used directly (`URI->new`, `->query_form`) and only arrives transitively.

Done when: `cpanfile` requires `LWP::Protocol::https` and `URI`.

